AI-native fuzz evidence: cross-schema RENAME loses auto-ID owner on cold reload
Date: 2026-07-25

Environment
-----------
TiDB RED binary:
  v9.0.0-beta.2.pre-2017-ged2376acc6
  commit ed2376acc6e0feeff9f3e2c38db489727933aa80
TiDB counterfactual source:
  commit 231dad5225f0d3c9cf38d4ab7ebc03a5326785c7
PD/TiKV:
  one PD and one real TiKV from agent-test TiUP nightly playground
Settings:
  Classic kernel
  tidb_enable_metadata_lock=ON
  AUTO_ID_CACHE=1
Faults:
  none

The warm TiDB created three tables, inserted generated IDs 1 and 2, and renamed
each table from ai_auto_reload_src to ai_auto_reload_dst. Before the cold TiDB
started, all three tables contained exactly IDs 1 and 2 and reported mode Normal.

Cold TiDB startup evidence
--------------------------
The TiDB process was started only after the RENAME statements and connected to
the same PD/TiKV. Its status endpoint reported:

  version=8.0.11-TiDB-v9.0.0-beta.2.pre-2017-ged2376acc6
  git_hash=ed2376acc6e0feeff9f3e2c38db489727933aa80

Its server log recorded a full InfoSchema load. Before any generated write:

  TABLE_NAME  AUTO_INCREMENT
  nonunique   0
  pk_insert   0
  pk_replace  0

RED cell A: explicit duplicate-key failure
------------------------------------------
SQL:
  INSERT INTO ai_auto_reload_dst.pk_insert(v) VALUES ('new-insert');

Result:
  ERROR 1062 (23000): Duplicate entry '2' for key 'pk_insert.PRIMARY'

Fresh rows:
  id  v
  1   old-1
  2   old-2

RED cell B: successful REPLACE silently overwrites an existing row
------------------------------------------------------------------
SQL:
  REPLACE INTO ai_auto_reload_dst.pk_replace(v) VALUES ('replacement');
  SELECT ROW_COUNT(), LAST_INSERT_ID();

Result:
  affected_rows  generated_id
  2              2

Fresh rows:
  id  v
  1   order-1
  2   replacement

The original row "2 order-2" was silently deleted. ADMIN CHECK TABLE returned
success because the resulting record/index state is structurally valid.

RED cell C: successful INSERT creates duplicate generated identity
------------------------------------------------------------------
SQL:
  INSERT INTO ai_auto_reload_dst.nonunique(v) VALUES ('new-cold-load');
  SELECT ROW_COUNT(), LAST_INSERT_ID();

Result:
  affected_rows  generated_id
  1              2

Fresh rows:
  id  v
  1   old-1
  2   new-cold-load
  2   old-2

Duplicate identity oracle:
  id  cnt
  2   2

ADMIN CHECK TABLE returned success.

GREEN owner counterfactual
--------------------------
The following temporary change was built as a full TiDB server from current
source and started cold against the same real cluster:

  func NewAllocatorsFromTblInfo(r Requirement, dbID int64, tblInfo *model.TableInfo) Allocators {
      if tblInfo.AutoIDSchemaID != 0 {
          dbID = tblInfo.AutoIDSchemaID
      }
      ...
  }

With the same RENAME and REPLACE schedule:

  affected_rows  generated_id
  1              3

Fresh rows:
  id  v
  1   order-1
  2   order-2
  3   replacement

The source change was removed after the run and the TiDB worktree was clean.

Post-RED deduplication
----------------------
Closed historical issue:
  https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/issues/55846
Historical merged fix:
  https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/pull/55847

The current result is recorded as a master regression of that root. The
successful REPLACE data-loss consumer is stronger than the historical
duplicate-key report.
